Project Overview

This project provides a step-by-step guide to installing the Windows operating system using a bootable USB flash drive.

Windows installation is an essential IT support task used when setting up a new computer, replacing a damaged operating system, or performing a clean installation.

«Documentation note: This is an instructional project. The infographic is an illustrative guide, not evidence of a personal installation.»

Installation Guide

"Windows Installation Guide" (windows-installation-guide.png)

Tools and Requirements

- Computer or laptop
- USB flash drive (8 GB or larger recommended)
- Windows installation media
- Reliable power supply
- Computer BIOS/UEFI boot menu

Installation Procedure

Step 1 — Prepare the Bootable USB

Create Windows installation media on a USB flash drive using an appropriate Windows installation-media tool.

Step 2 — Connect the USB Drive

Insert the bootable USB flash drive into the computer.

Step 3 — Access the Boot Menu

Restart the computer and use the manufacturer's boot-menu key to select the USB drive.

Step 4 — Start Windows Setup

Select the installation language, time format, and keyboard layout. Continue to Windows Setup.

Step 5 — Install Windows

Follow the installation instructions and select the appropriate installation option and destination drive.

«Important: A clean installation can erase existing files. Back up important data and confirm the correct destination drive before proceeding.»

Step 6 — Complete Initial Setup

Allow the installation to finish, then complete the initial Windows configuration.

Troubleshooting Considerations

Common issues during Windows installation include:

- USB drive not appearing in the boot menu
- Computer refusing to boot from USB
- Windows Setup not detecting the storage drive
- Installation interruptions
- Incorrect BIOS/UEFI boot settings

Expected Outcome

A successful installation should allow the computer to start Windows and proceed to the initial desktop setup.

